 "lines": {
  "StoryPrints finds the edges for you and outlines the photo in lime.": "8de03993e14c",
  "If the outline is right, tap Accept crop.": "897e25eaab8b",
  "The photo is cropped and ready to save.": "cb7851d41a12",
  "Use the arrows at the top to move to the next photo.": "ef3fe613c560",
  "If an edge is out, tap Adjust.": "c1144a4b5598",
  "Then tap just inside the photo, close to where its edge really is.": "9a79f76d5644",
  "StoryPrints looks there and snaps the line to it. Try this first, as it’s often all you need.": "790a6b595049",
  "If it says No edge there, drag the line instead. Then tap Apply Crop.": "70dbdce2e2e6",
  "You can also drag a corner or a side. A magnifier shows it close up under your finger.": "042446ca682c",
  "For fine control, tap the sliders button at the top right.": "66b961b35170",
  "Its buttons move the whole outline, or one edge in or out, in coarse or fine steps.": "bf656ef12c09",
  "Undo steps back, and Zoom takes a closer look.": "42a4db0c9186",
  "When it’s right, tap Apply Crop.": "ce105c3329b2"
